================================================================================
FILE DISABLED: merid_core/kalshi/execution_pipeline.py
================================================================================

STATUS:      QUARANTINED (T-001 Zero-Trust Audit)
REASON:      Parallel execution engine that bypasses ALL safety gates
HARDENED:    2026-04-23

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BYPASS RISK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This module is a PARALLEL execution engine that directly calls the Kalshi REST
API via merid_core.kalshi.rest_client, completely bypassing:

  - order_router.route_order_async() (canonical order routing)
  - GlobalRiskGuard (1-2% bankroll cap enforcement)
  - Top3BatchManager (top-3 allocation gate)
  - PreTradeGate (lease acquisition + deduplication)
  - Execution gate (kill switches, circuit breakers)
  - VenueGate (venue health checks)
  - Risk manager (position limits, daily loss limits)
  - Deployment controller (mode enforcement)

When MERID_NATS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true, this module:
  1. Consumes OrderIntents from NATS event bus
  2. Performs local (not canonical) risk checks
  3. Calls rest_client.create_order() directly via asyncio.to_thread()
  4. Updates local position tracking
  5. Publishes execution outcomes

This allows trades to execute OUTSIDE the canonical 9-gate execution path.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCTION HARDENING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The module now requires BOTH:
  1. MERID_NATS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true (legacy flag)
  2. MERID_ALLOW_EXECUTION_PIPELINE_BYPASS=1 (new hardening flag)

Without MERID_ALLOW_EXECUTION_PIPELINE_BYPASS, the module raises RuntimeError
at import time, completely disabling the bypass path.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCEPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To enable this bypass (NOT RECOMMENDED):

  export MERID_ALLOW_EXECUTION_PIPELINE_BYPASS=1
  export MERID_NATS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CANONICAL PATH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For legitimate order execution, use:

  POST /api/v1/kalshi/orders  →  kalshi_api.py  →  order_router.route_order_async()
  
or

  KalshiContinuousTrader  →  CTExecutionAdapter  →  order_router.route_order_async()

These paths enforce:
  - GlobalRiskGuard (max 1-2% bankroll allocation)
  - Top3BatchManager (top-3 edges only)
  - PreTradeGate (lease + deduplication)
  - Execution gate / kill switches
  - Full audit trail via decision_trace_id

